[21.3, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"run live analytical query on large sales dataset in BigQuery\"}\r\n"]
[22.1, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n"]
[22.9, "o", "**Google BigQuery MCP Server** is the right tool \u2014 it executes SQL queries and analyzes analytical data in BigQuery (bigquery.mcp.google.com/server.json).\r\n\r\n**One catch:** it's a Tier 3 tool, so it needs GCP authentication, and you don't have any set up right now (no gcloud CLI, ADC, or service account). Before you can query that 100GB dataset you'd need to either:\r\n- Install gcloud and run `gcloud auth application-default login`, or\r\n- Point to a service account / ADC credentials\r\n\r\nNote the free tier covers 1TB of query processing per month. If you'd rather skip GCP auth entirely, the BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines skill is available offline to help you write efficient analytical queries. Want me to set up the auth path?\r\n"]
[23.7, "o", "\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
