[34.586, "o", "\u001b[0;36m> using podman container \u00b7 asking opencode \u00b7 using deepseek-v4-flash-free\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[35.386, "o", "\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[36.186, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query a public BigQuery dataset with SQL\"}\r\n"]
[36.986, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n"]
[37.079, "o", "The best tool is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) \u2014 it executes SQL queries, inspects schemas, and explores public datasets. Let me check your auth status since it requires GCP credentials.\r\n"]
[37.879, "o", "The **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** is the tool for this \u2014 it executes SQL queries and explores public datasets.\r\n\r\nHowever, it requires GCP auth (Tier 3), and your system has **no gcloud CLI or credentials** currently. To use it you'd need to onboard:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt has a free tier (1TB query processing/month) for public datasets. The no-auth fallback (`bigquery-guidelines` skill) only offers SQL optimization guidance, not actual query execution.\r\n\r\nWant me to record this decision so you're not asked again, or proceed with onboarding?\r\n"]
[38.679, "o", "\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
