[48.767, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.821, "o", "================================================================================\r\n\ud83d\ude80 LAUNCHING OPENCODE REAL AGENT E2E TEST RUNNER\r\n\u2022 Container Image: localhost/ard-opencode:latest\r\n\u2022 Repo Path:       /usr/local/google/home/alanblount/Workspaces/open-source/ard-plugin-exploration\r\n"]
[48.821, "o", "================================================================================\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 1: Pure Public Discovery (Tier 0 Zero-Auth Counterpoint)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[49.621, "o", "Here's what I found:\r\n\r\n**SQL Query Optimization**\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:skills:bigquery-guidelines` \u2014 SQL optimization, partitioning/clustering, window functions, schema design (Tier 0, ready now)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:skills:database-design` \u2014 Cloud SQL/AlloyDB/Spanner tuning, indexing, connection pooling, migration (Tier 0, ready now)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery` \u2014 execute/analyze queries live (Tier 3, needs `gcloud auth application-default login`)\r\n\r\n**Zero-Trust Security**\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:skills:well-architected-security` \u2014 zero-trust architecture, IAM least-privilege, network perimeters, encryption (Tier 0, ready now)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:skills:gke-architecture` \u2014 network policy hardening, Gateway API (Tier 0, ready now)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:skills:firebase-architecture` \u2014 Firestore security rules (Tier 0, ready now)\r\n\r\nBest picks for your needs: the **BigQuery SQL guidelines** + **Well-Architected Security** skills \u2014 both Tier 0, run offline immediately with no GCP auth needed. Want me to load their full best-practice guidance?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"SQL query optimization best practices and performance tuning for databases\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"zero-trust security architecture design best practices\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 1 Passed: OpenCode returned Tier 0 skills with zero auth friction.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 2: Cloud Intent -> User Opts Out ('No with an opt out')\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[50.421, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) \u2014 it executes SQL directly on BigQuery and includes dry-run/cost estimation for a 100GB dataset. It needs GCP auth (Tier 3).\r\n\r\nCurrently not authenticated on this system (`no_gcloud`). To enable it, run `gcloud auth application-default login` (free tier covers 1TB of query processing/month). If you'd rather avoid GCP setup, the `bigquery-guidelines` skill can optimize your query offline.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"Run live analytical SQL queries on a 100GB sales dataset in BigQuery\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[51.221, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Opt-Out Response) ---\r\nOpt-out set. GCP tools will be filtered out going forward.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_set_preference {\"mode\":\"opt_out\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 2 Passed: OpenCode asked to log into GCP, user opted out, and GCP was silenced.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 3: Cloud Intent -> User Onboards ('Yes') -> Easy Onboarding\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[52.021, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) can do this \u2014 execute SQL, inspect schemas, explore public datasets.\r\n\r\nHowever, it requires GCP auth (Tier 3), and your system currently has **no gcloud CLI, service account, or ADC** configured. You'd need to install `gcloud` and run `gcloud auth application-default login` first (free tier: 1TB query / month).\r\n\r\nIf you'd rather avoid GCP auth entirely, the **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines Skill** (no auth) can still help write/optimize the query, but can't execute it.\r\n\r\nWant me to record your decision and set up GCP auth, or skip GCP for now?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query a public BigQuery dataset SQL\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[52.821, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Onboarding Instructions) ---\r\nI'll set up Google Cloud authentication. First, let me check the environment for installing the gcloud CLI.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"authentication login setup for Google Cloud MCP servers\"}\r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1m! \u001b[0mpermission requested: external_directory (/etc/*); auto-rejecting\r\n\u001b[0m\u2717 \u001b[0mcat /etc/os-release 2>/dev/null | head -5; echo \"---\"; which curl wget python3 apt dnf yum 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; ls ~/google-cloud-sdk 2>/dev/null && echo \"sdk dir exists\" || echo \"no sdk dir\" failed\r\n\u001b[91m\u001b[1mError: \u001b[0mThe user rejected permission to use this specific tool call.\r\n\r\n"]
[52.821, "o", "\u2705 Scenario 3 Passed: OpenCode facilitated easy GCP login onboarding.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea TEST 4: Complete ARD & OpenCode Unit and Scenario Suite\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[52.988, "o", "test_canonical_urn_format (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_canonical_urn_format)\r\nVerify all entries in ai-catalog.json strictly use canonical urn:ai: FQDN format. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_1_service_account_active (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_1_service_account_active)\r\nScenario 1: System has GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS pointing to a valid SA key. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_2_user_adc_active (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_2_user_adc_active)\r\nScenario 2: System has standard application_default_credentials.json. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_3_gcloud_installed_unauthenticated (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_3_gcloud_installed_unauthenticated)\r\nScenario 3: gcloud is in PATH, but no credentials are saved. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_4_bare_system_no_gcloud (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_4_bare_system_no_gcloud)\r\nScenario 4: Bare system without gcloud or GCP credentials (offline/clean). ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_5_user_opt_out_mode (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_5_user_opt_out_mode)\r\nScenario 5: User preference set to 'opt_out' -> Tier >= 3 tools are completely excluded. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_6_fallback_skills_and_api_keys (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_6_fallback_skills_and_api_keys)\r\nScenario 6: Verify API key detection (Gemini) and fallback skill links. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_7_multi_runtime_preferences (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_7_multi_runtime_preferences)\r\nScenario 7: Preferences work in ADK / ephemeral runtimes via env vars & memory. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_a_opt_out_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_a_opt_out_flow)\r\nScenario A: ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_b_gcloud_onboarding_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_b_gcloud_onboarding_flow)\r\nScenario B: ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_c_service_account_onboarding_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_c_service_account_onboarding_flow)\r\nScenario C: ... ok\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nRan 11 tests in 0.020s\r\n\r\nOK\r\n\r\n\u2705 Test 4 Passed: All 11 unit and scenario tests passed.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83d\udcca OPENCODE E2E SUMMARY: 4 PASSED, 0 FAILED\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
